\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {85}{\ignorespaces Polycomb silencing operates as a feedback-amplified two-mark system: PRC2 writes H3K27me3, which recruits more PRC2 (positive feedback) and recruits canonical PRC1 (via CBX) which writes H2AK119ub. Variant PRC1 acts upstream at unmethylated CpG islands and seeds H2AK119ub which itself recruits PRC2. The mutual reinforcement explains how Polycomb domains span hundreds of kilobases and persist through cell divisions.}}{391}{figure.caption.235}\protected@file@percent }
