\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {165}{\ignorespaces Oxygen delivery from lung to tissue and the Bohr effect. In the lungs (high PO\$\_2\$), haemoglobin loads O\$\_2\$ to 97\% saturation. In tissues (lower PO\$\_2\$), O\$\_2\$ is released. The Bohr effect rightward shift of the dissociation curve in metabolically active tissues (low pH, high CO\$\_2\$, high temperature) enhances O\$\_2\$ delivery where it is most needed.}}{691}{figure.caption.349}\protected@file@percent }
